  "ms": "Knowledge 1, Application 2, Analysis 2\nThree-firm concentration ratio is the sum of the largest market share of the biggest three firms as a proportion of the whole market (1) Calculations e.g.\n• 2681+1025+648 = 4354 (1)\n• 50+40+30+3748 = 3868 (1)\n• 8222 (1)\n• 4354/8222 (1) = 0.53 (5)\nAnswer = 52.96% Award 5 marks for correct answer (52.96) N.B. allow 52-53 or 0.53:1 (5) N.B. Maximum of 4 marks if no correct answer given e.g. 0.53 (4)",
