  "marks": 5,
  "section": "A",
  "text": "According to the Bank of England, the UK's marginal propensity to consume is estimated to be 0.64. paper/2017/.pdf?)\n(a) Using the information above, calculate the total reduction in the UK's GDP from a fall in government spending of £20 million.\n(4)\n(b) Which one of the following is an injection into the circular flow of income?\n(1)\nA Imports\nB Investment\nC Savings\nD Taxation",
  "ms": "(a)\nApplication 3, Analysis 1\nMultiplier formula= 1 / (1 – MPC) (1) = 1 / (1 –0.64) OR = 1 /0.36 (1) Value of the multiplier = 2.7 recurring OR 2.8 (1) 2.7 recurring X £20m (1) = £55.6m Award full marks for correct answer Award up to 3 marks if no correct answer NB Allow range (-)£55m to (-)£56m NB 3 marks if million missing\n\n(b)\nThe only correct answer is B\nA is not correct because imports are a withdrawal from the circular flow\nC is not correct because savings are a withdrawal from the circular flow\nD is not correct because taxation is a withdrawal from the circular flow",
