  "text": "Explain the difference between a positive and a normative statement, using an example of each from Extract A.",
  "ms": "Knowledge\nUp to 2marks, points might include:\n• positive statement e.g. statement of fact (1)\n• normative statement e.g. value judgement, moral, ethical (1)\nApplication:\n2 marks for data (1+1):\n• Positive example (1) e.g. o ‘removal of the 45% tax band’ o ‘1.25 % rise in national insurance was implemented’ o ‘already raised them from 0.1% in 2021 to 2.25% by September 2022’ o ‘Britain’s poorest households would have lost £7.56 a year’\n• Normative example (1) e.g. o ‘wrong time to do this’ o ‘an unfair decision at the time’\nAnalysis (1 mark) for linked development e.g.\n• can / cannot be tested (1)\n• subjective / objective (1)\nKnowledge 2, Application 2, Analysis 2,",
