  "q": "1",
  "part": "a",
  "marks": 5,
  "section": "A",
  "text": "With reference to Figure 1 and Extract A, explain what is meant by ‘price inelastic demand’ (line 8).",
  "ms": "Knowledge/implicit understanding and analysis:\nup to 3 marks e.g.\n• The percentage change in quantity demanded is less responsive to a change in price (1)\n• Is relatively low e.g. between 0 and -1 (or 0 and 1) / PED<1 (1)\n• Diagram showing price inelastic demand (1)\n• An increase in price will result in an increase in total revenue (1)\n• Reference to a characteristic e.g necessity, small proportion of income, few substitutes (1)\nApplication: up to 2 marks e.g.\n• UK consumers use gas for 85% of central\nheating/’are some of the biggest user of gas’ (1)\n• Gas generates a third of UK electricity (1)\n• There is no substitute for energy, at least in the\nshort run (1)\n• Calculation of price change as percentage or\npercentage points (1)\n• Rise from around 50p per therm in Feb 2021 to (5)\n352p per therm in Dec 2021 (1)\n• ‘An almost perfect example of price inelastic demand’ (Extract A lines 7-8)",
